                "submission_id": "submission:correctness-review:1:d2a7bafa",
                "summary": "Hold logic violates AC1 (a hand lost for single frames never turns the frame orange). src/recognise/recognise.ts:390-391 adopts whatever count arrives on the first frame after SEEN_HOLD_MS, not a count that held. Repro (scratch test with the repo's fakeCamera/fakeTime): two hands, then one hand for ~330 ms, then one empty frame, then one hand gives onSeen [2,...,2,0,1], so the frame goes orange for one frame. Fix: while lowerSince is set, track the highest count seen since then (e.g. own.lowerMax = max(lowerMax, hands)), and when the hold ends show that value and not the current frame; restart the hold if the frame is still below it. Add a test for 2 -> held 1 -> single 0 frame at hold expiry. Tick math checked and correct: deadline-derived count, next wake at the next second boundary, late-timer case right, left<=1 stops rescheduling, stopCamera cancels tick, press guard and the recording time limit unchanged. 37/37 tests pass after build. Non-blocking: recognise.ts:373, a timer that fires a few ms early shows the same count again and reschedules 1 ms later; harmless.",
                "task_id": "NG-46",
